2725+ 69F2              ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2726+ 69F2              ; search_by_Busy_fast
2727+ 69F2              ; Fast case-insensitive substring search for a name fully contained in the
2728+ 69F2              ; currently mapped 16K directory page.
2729+ 69F2              ;
2730+ 69F2              ; IN:  HL = name start, BC = 16-bit name length
2731+ 69F2              ;      pattern = INPBUFF, pattern length = value patched into txtlen+1
2732+ 69F2              ; OUT: Z = found, NZ = not found
2733+ 69F2              ;
2734+ 69F2              ; This is deliberately close to the original Busy FIND: the inner compare uses
2735+ 69F2              ; the Z80 CPI instruction.  The pattern has already been converted to lower
2736+ 69F2              ; case once by find_items, so only the source character needs convert here.
2737+ 69F2              ;
2738+ 69F2              ; Bugfix against the old search_by_Busy: after a failed PARTIAL match DE is
2739+ 69F2              ; restored to the exact candidate start and advanced by ONE byte.  Overlapping
2740+ 69F2              ; matches therefore cannot be skipped.
2741+ 69F2              ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2742+ 69F2              ; --- DOKUMENTACE CZ: search_by_Busy_fast ---
2743+ 69F2              ; Ucel: Vyhledá podřetězec bez rozlišení velikosti písmen v jedné bance.
2744+ 69F2              ; Vstup: HL = jméno, BC = délka; INPBUFF = vzor převedený na malá písmena, txtlen+1 = jeho
2745+ 69F2              ;   délka.
2746+ 69F2              ; Vystup: Z = shoda, NZ = nenalezeno.
2747+ 69F2              ; Meni: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC'; IX a IY zachovány.
