2806+ 6A2B              ; search_by_Busy_dir_slow
2807+ 6A2B              ; Fully bank-safe fallback. It is used only when a file name itself crosses a
2808+ 6A2B              ; #FFFF -> #C000 directory-page boundary. Such names are rare, so paging cost
2809+ 6A2B              ; no longer slows down every ordinary FIND operation.
2810+ 6A2B              ;
2811+ 6A2B              ; One-character FIND is handled before this fallback and compares only the
2812+ 6A2B              ; first character.  This slow path therefore normally handles 2+ character
